From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:37:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add dmc agent-hook for Muse Code and Claude Code turns

`dmc agent-hook <muse-code|claude-code> <event>` finds the workspace from
the payload cwd, begins a labelled checkpoint with agent context on
UserPromptSubmit, and closes it on Stop/StopFailure/SessionEnd (and Muse
Interrupt) only when this agent and session own it. Ownership is checked
under the same workspace lock as the close via CheckpointService.closeActive,
which also records the transcript size and SHA-256. A missed Stop is closed
by the next prompt; foreign checkpoints are left alone with a stderr warning.
Busy locks are retried briefly. The command always exits 0, never writes
stdout, and falls back to the session env when stdin is empty or invalid.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TZntz1MeHVb13u53UKzx8U
